@startuml btrie-trie-node-layout
' ============================================================================
' btrie-trie-node-layout.puml — the B-trie trie node (512 bytes = 128 × 4-byte ptrs).
' Source: docs/theory/disk-tries/02-b-trie.md (Askitis & Zobel 2009), § Page Layout.
' Replaces the ASCII byte-layout box with a compact, colored, viewBox'd byte-field.
' Color key:  blue #BBDEFB  child pointers (one per ASCII char)
'             grey #ECEFF1  elision of the 124 middle pointers
' ============================================================================
skinparam defaultFontSize 14
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam defaultFontName "DejaVu Sans"
skinparam rectangle {
  BorderColor #37474F
  FontColor #212121
  BorderThickness 1.2
}
skinparam noteFontSize 13
skinparam TitleFontSize 15

title B-trie trie node — 512 bytes = 128 × 4-byte pointers

rectangle "bytes **0..3**    Pointer[0] — child for char 0 (NUL)" as R0 #BBDEFB
rectangle "bytes **4..7**    Pointer[1] — child for char 1" as R1 #BBDEFB
rectangle "        ⋮        Pointer[2 .. 126]  (124 more)" as R2 #ECEFF1
rectangle "bytes **508..511**    Pointer[127] — child for char 127 (DEL)" as R3 #BBDEFB

R0 -[hidden]down- R1
R1 -[hidden]down- R2
R2 -[hidden]down- R3

note bottom
  **Pointer encoding** (4 bytes each):
  MSB = 0 → bucket (block number) · MSB = 1 → trie node (block number, MSB set)
  all zeros → null pointer.  16 trie nodes fit in one 8 KB block.
end note
@enduml
